{% comment %}
  Echoes the Akeneo color code parsed from a media/image filename, or nothing.

  Akeneo sync filename convention (alt text is empty, so the filename is the
  only color carrier): {sha1}_{product_code}_{color_code}__{shot}[_{uuid}].ext
    5671d2d0..._2800BC_192_953__01.jpg  -> 192_953   (Loewenweiss, 2-segment)
    a9f5f34c..._X03_339__01.jpg         -> 339       (FitFlop)
    848bcd3c..._SB8985_001__01.jpg      -> 001       (Sweaty Betty)

  The double underscore before the shot number produces an empty part, which
  marks a convention-conforming filename and terminates the color code.
  Anything else (videos, models, manually uploaded images) echoes nothing and
  is treated as color-neutral.

  NOTE vs. the reuse-source project: SB's equivalent assumes the code is
  exactly one part (`parts[2]`, guarded by `parts[3] == blank`). That breaks on
  OB's two-segment Loewenweiss codes (`192_953`), so this version scans for the
  empty part instead and joins everything between the product code and it.

  Accepts (one of):
  - media: {Object} product media object
  - image_src: {String} an image src, when you have an image rather than media

  Usage (capture the output to branch on it):
    {%- capture code -%}{%- render 'ob-media-color-code', media: media -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign src = image_src | default: media.preview_image.src
  assign fname = src | split: '/' | last | split: '?' | first
  assign parts = fname | split: '_'

  assign stop_idx = 0
  for part in parts
    if part == blank and forloop.index0 > 2
      assign stop_idx = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor

  if stop_idx > 2
    assign code = ''
    for part in parts
      if forloop.index0 > 1 and forloop.index0 < stop_idx
        if code == blank
          assign code = part
        else
          assign code = code | append: '_' | append: part
        endif
      endif
    endfor
    echo code
  endif
-%}
